# Shell scripts must keep LF endings wherever they are checked out.
#
# ACC-127: backend/scripts/pre-deploy.sh runs in an Alpine container as the
# deployment's migration step. With CRLF, `/bin/sh` reads the shebang line as
# `/bin/sh\r` and the script fails in a way that reads as a missing
# interpreter rather than a line-ending problem. This repository is developed
# on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule the guarantee rests
# on each developer's local git configuration rather than on the repository.
*.sh text eol=lf
